{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Plan AC2 reworded during implementation, with evidence. On git 2.56 a 60-day reflog entry whose commit is an ancestor of the tip was pruned under default settings, and with gc.reflogExpire=never alone a 45-day unreachable entry was kept, so a test cannot assert the 90-day/30-day split the docs describe. The step passes no expiry value, so the tests now prove: stale entries expire, recent ones stay, and the repository's own gc.reflogExpire* settings govern. Re-running the plan review on the revised description."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1794479357870902001,"uuid":"219f221f-d508-4b93-87c7-cfd0c0143108"}